    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 4th centers on a high-upside matchup against Nick Pivetta and the Boston rotation, specifically targeting the favorable pitching profiles of Bello and Nelson. **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) remains our anchor today; his elite BvP history against Bello (25 PA) combined with a massive +14% platoon edge makes him our most dangerous weapon for both power and counting stats. **Kyle Tucker** (74.31) and **Andy Pages** (68.56) also project as strong starts against Nelson; while their lineup positions are currently pending, their base projections remain robust enough to anchor the outfield provided they hit in the top half of the order as expected.\n\nThe decision-making process at the margins was difficult today, particularly regarding **Jackson Merrill** (51.86). Despite facing the formidable Zack Wheeler\u2014an elite arm that typically warrants a benching\u2014**Jackson Merrill** retains a starting nod due to his dynamic platoon advantage and a projected spot in the heart of the order. Conversely, **Miguel Andujar** (35.83) was our closest call for the bench; he fell well below our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable platoon matchup against Wheeler, which effectively neutralized his base projection. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.75) carries a marginal score, he stays in the lineup to preserve game caps, though his utility is capped by a difficult outing against Chris Sale. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our current depth limited as we navigate this stretch without their production.",
